wireguard-mc
============

This package provides a customized wireguard-go that speaks WireGuard over
TCP with optional Minecraft protocol camouflage. Both tunnel ends must use
this binary (not kernel WireGuard / stock UDP wireguard-go).

Key generation (same as wg)
---------------------------

  umask 077
  wireguard-go genkey | tee private.key | wireguard-go pubkey > public.key
  wireguard-go genpsk > psk.key

Quick start (systemd)
---------------------

1. Edit /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-transport.json
   (loginPluginSecret must match on both ends).
2. Copy and edit the interface config:
     cp /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf.example /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf
     chmod 600 /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf
3. Enable and start the service:
     sudo wireguard-go install          # interface wg0
     sudo wireguard-go install wg0      # same
4. Status / logs:
     systemctl status wireguard-go@wg0
     journalctl -u wireguard-go@wg0 -f

After apt upgrade, all enabled/active wireguard-go@ instances are restarted
automatically so the new binary is picked up.

Stop and remove the service unit instance:
     sudo wireguard-go uninstall
     sudo wireguard-go uninstall --purge   # also delete configs

Foreground (debug):
     sudo LOG_LEVEL=verbose /usr/bin/wireguard-go -f wg0

Binary path: /usr/bin/wireguard-go
Config dir:  /etc/wireguard/
Unit file:   /lib/systemd/system/wireguard-go@.service
